VulkanGPU — reusable C++17 VulkanEngine GPU resources and computation.
  gpu/gpu.hpp            umbrella public API
  gpu/buffer.*           owned GPU buffer and host-visible uploads
  gpu/image.*            owned images/views
  gpu/shader.*           SPIR-V modules
  gpu/descriptors.*      arbitrary descriptor bindings
  gpu/pipeline.*         pipeline layout
  gpu/compute.*          generic compute and indirect dispatch
  gpu/transfer.*         buffer copy/fill
  gpu/upload.hpp         asynchronous fenced staging batches
  gpu/texture_cache.*    RGBA8 texture residency, caching and views
  gpu/graph.*            explicit ordered passes/barriers
  gpu/culler.*           frustum-sphere culling and instance compaction
  gpu/shaders/cull.comp  reference GLSL culling shader

Host initializes VulkanEngine and owns queues, swapchain, frame fences.
Texture cache replacement and retirement require no in-flight GPU reads.
Culling shader is supplied as compiled SPIR-V at initialization; consumers
can compile the bundled GLSL shader or use a binary compatible variant.
Culling descriptors require binding 0 transforms, 1 sphere bounds,
2 visible compact IDs, 3 indirect arguments. Call begin/dispatch/end
in order, outside render passes. Culling is not occlusion culling.
